Functions:
1. Name: Send Email
Description: Sends an email to one or more recipients.
Input: 
{
  "personalizations": {
    "required": "Object",
    "description": "An array of objects containing the recipient's email address, name, and any custom data you want to include in the email."
  },
  "from": {
    "required": "Object",
    "description": "An object containing the sender's email address and name."
  },
  "subject": {
    "required": "String",
    "description": "The subject of the email."
  },
  "content": {
    "required": "Array",
    "description": "An array of objects containing the email's content. Each object should contain a type (text or html) and a value (the actual content)."
  },
  "attachments": {
    "required": "Array",
    "description": "An array of objects containing the email's attachments. Each object should contain a filename and a base64-encoded content."
  }
}
Output: Returns a 202 Accepted response if the email was successfully queued for delivery.

2. Name: Retrieve Email Statistics
Description: Retrieves statistics for emails sent through Sendgrid.
Input: 
{
  "start_date": {
    "required": "String",
    "description": "The start date for the statistics in YYYY-MM-DD format."
  },
  "end_date": {
    "required": "String",
    "description": "The end date for the statistics in YYYY-MM-DD format."
  },
  "aggregated_by": {
    "required": "String",
    "description": "The time period to aggregate the statistics by. Valid values are day, week, or month."
  },
  "categories": {
    "required": "Array",
    "description": "An array of categories to filter the statistics by."
  }
}
Output: Returns an array of objects containing statistics for each time period and category.

3. Name: Retrieve Email Bounces
Description: Retrieves a list of email bounces.
Input: 
{
  "start_time": {
    "required": "Integer",
    "description": "The start time for the bounces in Unix timestamp format."
  },
  "end_time": {
    "required": "Integer",
    "description": "The end time for the bounces in Unix timestamp format."
  },
  "status": {
    "required": "String",
    "description": "The status of the bounces to retrieve. Valid values are processed, deferred, and bounced."
  }
}
Output: Returns an array of objects containing information about each bounce.

4. Name: Retrieve Email Blocks
