Function_Description.sendGif:
Send a GIF to another user through a supported messaging platform
Parameters: {"gif_id": "string. The unique ID of the GIF to send.", "source_post_url": "string. The URL of the web page where the GIF was originally found.", "tags": "Array[string]. An array of tags associated with the GIF.", "rating": "string. The content rating of the GIF (e.g. 'g', 'pg-13')."}
Output: A success message indicating that the GIF was sent successfully.
 - Format: application/json
 - Structure: Object{message}

Function_Description.components:
The detailed output format for the tools is outlined below:
#Gif: Object{type, id, url, title, rating, images: Object{original: Object{url, width, height}, fixed_height: Object{url, width, height}, fixed_width: Object{url, width, height}}}
#GifSendRequest: Object{gif_id, source_post_url, tags: Array[string], rating}
#Category: Object{name, gif_count, subcategories: Array[string]}

