NLDocumentation:
imageModeration: Utilizes machine learning algorithms to classify and identify images based on their content, while blocking unwanted images or blurring out sensitive or offensive material.
Parameters: {"image": "Required. string. The base64-encoded image data.", "categories": "Array[string]. A list of categories to classify the image into. If not provided, the API will classify the image into all available categories."}
Output: The moderation result of the image, including whether it is safe or not, and any blocked or blurred regions.
 - Format: application/json
 - Structure: Object{status, categories: Array[Object{name, score}], moderation: Object{safe, blocked_regions: Array[Object{x, y, width, height}], blurred_regions: Array[Object{x, y, width, height}]}}
imageCensoring: Allows users to censor specific parts of an image, such as faces, to protect the privacy of individuals or prevent unauthorized usage.
Parameters: {"image": "Required. string. The base64-encoded image data.", "regions": "Required. Array[Object{type: string. The type of region to censor, such as 'face' or 'text'., x: integer. The x-coordinate of the top-left corner of the region., y: integer. The y-coordinate of the top-left corner of the region., width: integer. The width of the region., height: integer. The height of the region.}. ]. A list of regions to censor, including their coordinates and type."}
Output: The base64-encoded image data with the specified regions censored.
 - Format: application/json
 - Structure: Object{status, image}

